<section
	class="openxhc-boundary"
	data-openxhc-system-boundary
	aria-labelledby="openxhc-boundary-title"
>
	<header class="openxhc-boundary__header">
		<p class="section-kicker">System boundary / offline first</p>
		<h2 id="openxhc-boundary-title">From captured motion to testable code</h2>
		<p>
			The project converts observations from a real CNC system into a native,
			falsifiable software model. Each stage narrows uncertainty before any
			future Linux control path can reach hardware.
		</p>
	</header>

	<ol class="openxhc-boundary__flow" aria-label="Validated OpenXHC workflow">
		<li data-boundary-step>
			<p aria-hidden="true">01</p>
			<h3>Owner-authorized captures</h3>
			<span>Real motion evidence retained privately and summarized safely.</span>
		</li>
		<li data-boundary-step>
			<p aria-hidden="true">02</p>
			<h3>Offline C++20 codec</h3>
			<span>Fixed-capacity parsing and encoding with no device-open path.</span>
		</li>
		<li data-boundary-step>
			<p aria-hidden="true">03</p>
			<h3>Byte-exact validator</h3>
			<span>Captured reports must reconstruct exactly, not just round-trip.</span>
		</li>
		<li data-boundary-step>
			<p aria-hidden="true">04</p>
			<h3>Coordinate comparison</h3>
			<span>Decoded positions are checked against observed machine coordinates.</span>
		</li>
	</ol>

	<div class="openxhc-boundary__evidence">
		<figure data-synthetic-validation>
			<picture>
				<source
					srcset="/media/openxhc/openxhc-validation-illustrative-640.webp 640w, /media/openxhc/openxhc-validation-illustrative-960.webp 960w, /media/openxhc/openxhc-validation-illustrative-1440.webp 1440w"
					sizes="(max-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 2rem), 62vw"
					type="image/webp"
				/>
				<img
					src="/media/openxhc/openxhc-validation-illustrative-640.webp"
					width="1440"
					height="960"
					loading="lazy"
					decoding="async"
					alt="Illustrative CNC evidence flow passing through offline validation stages before a hard machine-control boundary."
				/>
			</picture>
			<figcaption>
				Illustrative model. Aggregate metrics are measured; no protocol bytes are shown.
			</figcaption>
		</figure>

		<aside data-future-boundary aria-labelledby="future-boundary-title">
			<p class="section-kicker">Deliberately outside the current artifact</p>
			<h3 id="future-boundary-title">Future integration boundary</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>USB transport</li>
				<li>Trajectory planning</li>
				<li>Safety supervision</li>
				<li>LinuxCNC HAL integration</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				The current result is a validated foundation, not a claim of autonomous
				machine control.
			</p>
		</aside>
	</div>
</section>

